**Isolate each `prepare()` call so one throwing preparer cannot skip the others.**

`cleanupStarted` is already `true` when the loop runs. If any registered `prepare()` throws, the exception leaves `prepareProcessSignalCleanup`. The remaining preparers then never run. The `force` array is lost, so no final SIGKILL sweep is returned.

`registerProcessSignalCleanup` is a shared extension point, so a future registrant can break the child cleanup in `src/shared/proc.ts`. The `proc.ts` preparer is safe today only because `terminateActiveChildrenOnExit` swallows its own errors.

Catch per preparer and continue.

<details>
<summary>Proposed fix</summary>

```diff
   for (const prepare of cleanups) {
-    const kill = prepare();
-    if (kill !== undefined) force.push(kill);
+    try {
+      const kill = prepare();
+      if (kill !== undefined) force.push(kill);
+    } catch {
+      // One failing preparer must not skip the remaining owners' cleanup.
+    }
   }
```
</details>

**Wrapper mislabels abort and non-contention errors as "still held after the waiter budget".**

The `catch` at Line 224 wraps every failure from the acquire block in the same message. That includes errors from `signal.throwIfAborted()` (Lines 207 and 212) and `delay(..., { signal })` (Line 220). It also includes non-`ELOCKED` filesystem errors such as `EACCES` and `ENOSPC`, which Line 219 rethrows.

Consequences:
- A caller that aborts gets a generic `Error` instead of an `AbortError`. A check such as `err.name === 'AbortError'` fails. The `GitMutex.withLock` doc says the signal "cancels queued acquisition".
- An operator who hits a permission or disk fault is told the lock is held. This sends the investigation in the wrong direction.

Rethrow abort errors unchanged. Use the "still held" text only for `ELOCKED`.

<details>
<summary>Proposed fix</summary>

```diff
       } catch (err) {
-        throw new Error(
-          `git-mutex: could not acquire '${config.lockPath}' — still held after the waiter budget (${String(retries)} retries, ~${String(budgetMs)} ms backoff floor at ${String(retryBaseMs)} ms base, stale window ${String(staleMs)} ms) — ${err instanceof Error ? err.message : String(err)}`,
-          { cause: err },
-        );
+        if (signal?.aborted === true) throw err;
+        const contended = err instanceof Error && 'code' in err && err.code === 'ELOCKED';
+        throw new Error(
+          `git-mutex: could not acquire '${config.lockPath}' — ${contended ? `still held after the waiter budget (${String(retries)} retries, ~${String(budgetMs)} ms backoff floor at ${String(retryBaseMs)} ms base, stale window ${String(staleMs)} ms)` : 'unexpected acquire fault'} — ${err instanceof Error ? err.message : String(err)}`,
+          { cause: err },
+        );
       }
```
</details>
